L001500	Although the expression in \eqref{eq:tsnapA_original} allows to compute the snap-through time for bifurcation buckling, it depends on the quantities $\check{r}_\text{B}$ and $\check{q}_\text{B}$, which are defined through infinite sums involving numerically computed eigenvalues and eigenfunctions. The numerical approximations involved in their computation can thus introduce significant errors. Here we show that the infinite sums for $\check{r}_\text{B}$ and $\check{q}_\text{B}$  can instead be expressed in terms of inner products of functions with closed-form analytical expressions.
L001501	We first introduce two functions $\vec{\varphi}_1$ and $\vec{\varphi}_2$ that are the solutions of the linear problems
L001502	\begin{subequations}\label{varphi eq}
L001503	\begin{align}
L001504	 \mathcal{L}\vec{\varphi}_1 &= \delta(\theta)\vec{F}, \\
L001505	 \mathcal{L}\vec{\varphi}_2 &= \mathcal{B}(\check{\vec{u}}_0^A,\check{\vec{u}}_0^A),
L001506	\end{align}
L001507	\end{subequations}
L001508	and for which an analytical form exists.  By writing those function via an eigenfunction expansions, we find that
L001509	\multig[phis]{
L001510	\vec{\varphi}_1(\theta) = \sum_{n\in\mathbb{S}}\frac{F_n}{\left(\omega_n^S\right)^2}\check{\boldsymbol{u}}_n^S,\\
L001511	\vec{\varphi}_2(\theta) = \sum_{n\in\mathbb{S}}\frac{\mathcal{B}_{00n}^{AAS}}{\left(\omega_n^S\right)^2}\check{\boldsymbol{u}}_n^S .
L001512	}
L001513	By comparing the forms \eqref{phis} with the ones in \eqref{asymmetric params}, the coefficients $\check{r}_\text{B}$ and $\check{q}_\text{B}$ can be rewritten in terms of integrals of analytical expressions as
L001514	\begin{align}\label{r_B ana}
L001515	    \check{r}_\text{B}= 2\sum_{n\in\mathbb{S}}\frac{F_n}{\left(\omega_n^S\right)^2}\mathcal{B}_{n00}^{SAA}
L001516	    = 2\left\langle\mathcal{B}(\vec{\varphi}_1,\vec{\check{u}}_0^A),\vec{\check{u}}_0^A\right\rangle
L001517	\end{align}
L001518	and
L001519	\begin{align}
L001520	    \check{q}_\text{B} = \mathcal{T}_{0000}^{AAAA} + 2\sum_{n\in\mathbb{S}}\frac{\mathcal{B}^{SAA}_{n00}\mathcal{B}^{AAS}_{00n}}{\left(\omega_n^S\right)^2}
L001521	    =\mathcal{T}_{0000}^{AAAA} +2 \left\langle \mathcal{B}\left(\vec{\varphi}_2,\check{\vec{u}}_0^A\right),\check{\vec{u}}_0^A\right\rangle.
L001522	\end{align}
