L001594	{\section{Overshooting the limit-point bifurcation}}\label{Sec:Overshoot}
L001595	{Numerical simulations reveal there is a small range of slenderness values $\lambda$ exceeding $\lambda_{\text{hill}}^{+}$ where the arch evolves symmetrically during snap-through and the snap-through time
L001596	is much smaller than that predicted for bifurcation buckling (see Fig.~1~(e) in the main text).
L001597	The dynamics in this region resemble snap-through associated with a limit-point bifurcation.}
L001598	
L001599	{For slenderness values
L001600	$\lambda > \lambda_{\text{hill}}^{+}$, the system exhibits two critical loads: one
L001601	associated with bifurcation buckling and one associated with limit-point buckling.
