L001603	for bifurcation buckling is only slightly less than the critical load for limit-point buckling.
L001604	Therefore, when the applied load is increased beyond the threshold for bifurcation buckling by an amount $\Delta P$,
L001605	the threshold for limit-point buckling can also be exceeded as depicted in Fig.~\ref{fig:Zoom}~(a).  We call this
L001606	`overshooting' the limit-point bifurcation.  When overshooting
L001607	occurs, the response of the system becomes dominated by the
L001608	limit-point bifurcation rather than the pitchfork bifurcation.
